 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+36}Ar|)1p+1n+{+34}Cl from J|p=0+ {+36}Ar ground state.               
 34CL c  1969Br21: a 45-MeV proton beam was produced from the Berkeley 88-Inch  
 34CL2c  Cyclotron. The target was 99.6%-enriched {+36}Ar gas. Reaction products
 34CL3c  were detected using a 155-|mm phosphorus-diffused silicon |DE          
 34CL4c  transmission counter and a 3.0-mm lithium-drifted silicon E counter    
 34CL5c  operated in coincidence, followed by a 0.5-mm lithium-drifted silicon  
 34CL6c  E-reject counter operated in anti-coincidence with the first two       
 34CL7c  counters to eliminate long-range particles. Measured |s(E({+3}He),|q). 
 34CL8c  Deduced levels, L-transfers, J, |p, and isospin. Also measured         
 34CL9c  {+36}Ar(p,t){+34}Ar and {+36}Ar(d,|a){+34}Cl.                          
 34CL cL $Selection rules used by 1969Br21 for direct two-particle transfer     
 34CL2cL reactions: {+36}Ar(p,t){+34}Ar transfers particles with T=1, S=0;      
 34CL3cL {+36}Ar(d,|a){+34}Cl transfers particles with T=0, S=1.                
 34CL4cL {+36}Ar(p,{+3}He){+34}Cl transfers particles with T=1, S=0 if the      
 34CL5cL transfer is direct two-particle transfer, |s(|q) of                    
 34CL6cL {+36}Ar(p,{+3}He){+34}Cl matches |s(|q) of the mirror state in {+34}Ar 
 34CL7cL populated by {+36}Ar(p,t){+34}Ar, and absent in {+36}Ar(d,|a){+34}Cl.  
